# The serial console carries the kernel's early boot, for a boot that never gets as far as the
# host's log port, and a panic; once Android has finished booting, nothing else. Every byte
# written to the emulated serial port traps out of the VM with the port's lock held, taking
# processor time from whatever else runs there, vsync and input among them.
#
# Console level 1 prints only emergencies; a panic raises the level itself, so its report
# still reaches the console. The kernel's other messages stay in its ring buffer, which logd
# reads (ro.logd.kernel) and `dsa logcat -b kernel` shows on demand.
#
# A system script, because only init itself may write the kernel's printk levels.
on property:sys.boot_completed=1
    write /proc/sys/kernel/printk 1
